traceability.evidence:
Key files and tests: - Story file exists: docs/stories/008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX.story.md - Dedicated test file for this story: tests/rules/auto-fix-behavior-008.test.ts - Header: "* Tests for: docs/stories/008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX.story.md
 * @story docs/stories/008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX.story.md
 * @req REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING ...
 * @req REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT ..." - For REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING (require-story-annotation): - Valid examples confirm already-annotated functions/methods are unchanged. - Invalid examples provide code and expected `output` showing `/** @story docs/stories/003.0-DEV-FUNCTION-ANNOTATIONS.story.md */` inserted before: - function declarations (`function autoFixMe() {}`) - function expressions (`const fnExpr = function() {};`) - class methods (`class C {
 method() {}
}`) - TS declare functions (`declare function tsDecl(): void;`) - TS interface method signatures (`interface D {
 method(): void;
}`) - For REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT (valid-annotation-format): - Valid example where story path already ends with `.story.md` is unchanged. - Invalid examples: - Input: `// @story docs/stories/005.0-DEV-ANNOTATION-VALIDATION.story` -> Output adds `.md`. - Input: `// @story docs/stories/005.0-DEV-ANNOTATION-VALIDATION` -> Output adds `.story.md`. - Jest test invocation for this file completed without reported failures: - Command: `npm test -- --runTestsByPath tests/rules/auto-fix-behavior-008.test.ts --verbose` - Output: > eslint-plugin-traceability@1.0.5 test > jest --ci --bail --runTestsByPath tests/rules/auto-fix-behavior-008.test.ts --verbose
Implementation for missing @story auto-fix (REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING, REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE, REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE): - src/rules/require-story-annotation.ts - JSDoc ties directly to this story and requirements: "@story docs/stories/008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX.story.md" and multiple "@req REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING / REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE / REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE" annotations. - meta: - fixable: "code" - hasSuggestions: true - messageId "missingStory" with actionable guidance. - create(context) wires in visitors from helpers that provide fixes. - src/rules/helpers/require-story-helpers.ts - Defines a simple, built-in template used for fixes: - const STORY_PATH = "docs/stories/003.0-DEV-FUNCTION-ANNOTATIONS.story.md"; - const ANNOTATION = `/** @story ${STORY_PATH} */`; - reportMissing(...): - Resolves function name. - Skips when hasStoryAnnotation(...) indicates an existing @story. - Uses context.report with `fix: createAddStoryFix(resolvedTarget)` and a suggestion using the same fix. - reportMethod(...) provides equivalent behavior for methods. - hasStoryAnnotation(...) aggregates multiple checks (JSDoc, preceding comments, parent chain, text-before heuristics) to avoid duplicate or unsafe fixes. - src/rules/helpers/require-story-core.ts - createAddStoryFix(target): returns a fixer that inserts `${ANNOTATION}
` before the chosen range (either the node or its export wrapper), touching only comment text. - createMethodFix(node): inserts `${ANNOTATION}
 ` before method nodes, preserving surrounding code and indentation. - No function bodies or runtime expressions are changed, only comments are added, satisfying safety and preservation requirements.
Implementation for format auto-fix (REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT, REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE, REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE): - src/rules/helpers/valid-annotation-utils.ts - getFixedStoryPath(original: string): - If `original` contains ".." -> returns null (avoid traversal). - If it already ends with ".story.md" -> returns null (no fix). - If it ends with ".story" -> returns `${original}.md`. - If it ends with ".md" but not `.story.md` -> replaces with `.story.md`. - Otherwise -> appends `.story.md`. - JSDoc explicitly references docs/stories/008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX.story.md and REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT / REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE / REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE. - src/rules/valid-annotation-format.ts - meta.fixable: "code" with JSDoc stating it is limited to safe suffix normalization per Story 008.0. - validateStoryAnnotation(...): - Trims and collapses whitespace. - If value matches configured pattern, returns (no error). - If value has internal whitespace, calls reportInvalidStoryFormat(...) (no fix). - Else computes `fixed = getFixedStoryPath(collapsed)` and, if `fixed` is non-null and matches pattern, calls reportInvalidStoryFormatWithFix(...); otherwise falls back to non-fixing error. - reportInvalidStoryFormatWithFix(...): - Uses createStoryFix(...) to locate just the @story path substring in the comment and then calls `fix: fixer.replaceTextRange(fixRange, fixed)`. - If createStoryFix(...) cannot safely derive a range, it calls reportInvalidStoryFormat(...) instead, avoiding unsafe changes. - createStoryFix(...): - Locates "@story" in the exact comment text. - Uses a regex to find the following path segment and computes precise offsets. - Returns a function that only replaces that substring, preserving all other comment text and whitespace.
Documentation (Acceptance: Documentation): - user-docs/api-reference.md - traceability/require-story-annotation: - Documents that with `--fix` the rule "inserts a single-line placeholder JSDoc `@story` annotation above missing functions, methods, TypeScript declare functions, and interface method signatures using a built-in template aligned with Story 008.0" and that it does not alter function bodies or runtime behavior. - Notes that template configurability and selective auto-fix behavior are planned but not yet implemented, matching the story’s "Not yet implemented" notes for REQ-AUTOFIX-TEMPLATE and REQ-AUTOFIX-SELECTIVE. - traceability/valid-annotation-format: - Describes auto-fix behavior as limited to safe `@story` path suffix normalization (e.g., adding `.md` or `.story.md`), implemented via `getFixedStoryPath` and `reportInvalidStoryFormatWithFix`, and explicitly states that directories, story names, and surrounding comment formatting are not changed.
Scope alignment: - The story’s "Requirements (Current Implementation or To Be Implemented)" section explicitly marks REQ-AUTOFIX-TEMPLATE and REQ-AUTOFIX-SELECTIVE as "Not yet implemented" and frames them as future enhancements. The checked acceptance criteria focus on the core auto-fix behaviors for missing @story and simple format issues, safety, integration, predictability, error handling, and documentation—all of which are implemented and evidenced by code and tests above.
